WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Choose the page from the sidebar
From the sidebar choose “Auto Reply”.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Choosing the channel
The WhatsApp, Telegram, Instagram and other buttons change the channel whose flow you are editing; each channel has its own flow and its own on/off switch.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Library filter: All and Steps
“All” shows every card, and “Steps” shows the single steps such as the welcome and the services menu.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Full flows filter
“Full flows” shows templates made of several linked steps. The + button on a card adds it straight to the diagram.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Add a ready-made flow
We press + on “Full customer service flow”. The welcome, menu, prices, order follow-up and transfer steps appear already linked.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Zoom out, zoom in and re-center
The − button zooms the diagram out, the + button zooms it in, and the ⌖ button restores the default zoom and position. These buttons don't change the steps' content.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Edit a step
Press a step card on the diagram to open its form. The step name only shows on the diagram, while the message text is what the customer sees.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Change the type and the link
The “Step type” list sets the action. “Link to step” sets what follows; you can also link by dragging from the dot on the step's side to the step you want.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Add and remove an option
In a list step write the question and the options. “Add option” creates a row, and × deletes the option. Each option has its own list to link the next step.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Move-step arrows
The left, right, up and down buttons move the step's position. You can also move the card by dragging it on the diagram.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Save the change and close
“Save changes” saves the step's content. “Close” or × closes the window. Check the save-success message before you carry on.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Delete the step
“Delete step” removes the step from the flow; review the flow and its links afterwards. We show it here on an extra training step only.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Turning on and off
The “Auto-reply off/on” switch turns the selected channel's flow on or off. Test from another account before turning it on for customers.
